    description: "[REVIEW 2026-11-01, PARTLY-STALE] Reviewed 2026-11-01 at dev 100b6fbb6e. The item names no language. Fixture run: Python module-level `f = real_target; f()` now emits calls caller -> real_target (fixed by 1aff4e7d51, WI-gulot, 2026-07-03, after this item was filed). Still dead-ending: JS `const jf = jsTarget; jf()` -> calls to jf:variable only; Python class-body `alias = meth` -> calls to K.alias:field; local `h = real_target; h()` (Python) and `const loc = jsTarget; loc()` (JS) -> references only, no calls edge. Go package-level aliases were fixed by WI-labik (98a5b50e98). (Original text below; the review entry in the thread has the evidence.)\n\nSplit out of WI-togop-hikog-domub-gofor-puriv-fakov-bojus-jozus's discussion (it blocks WI-togop's closure). The tool processes function aliasing / name rebinding (f = g) statically but mis-resolves the alias, dead-ending the call graph: a call through the alias is not connected to the real target. A genuine call-graph correctness defect, distinct from WI-togop's limits.not_captured disclosure concern. Strategy Wave-0 B4."  # c7b7
